WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.320
Like a lot of fans of the SCP Foundation universe,&nbsp;
we’ve often theorized about the coolest Vs battles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.240
we can imagine here on SCP Explained. Whether&nbsp;
it’s warring gods, researchers, or anomalies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.080
who doesn’t love a good fight? But ever&nbsp;
since we’ve started taking mandatory anger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.320
management counseling after the pudding&nbsp;
cup incident in the Site-19 Break Room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.120
we’ve decided to reorient our focus a little.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.960
That’s why today, we’re going to&nbsp;
talk about teamwork and friendship.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.640
Namely, which teams, friendships, and alliances&nbsp;
would lead to the deadliest outcomes. Hey, look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.080
nobody’s perfect, but together, certain anomalous&nbsp;
duos do have the power to be perfectly deadly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.800
That’s why we’re going to give you a whirlwind&nbsp;
rundown of our ultimate matches made in Hell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.600
These are the deadliest SCP&nbsp;
combinations we could possibly find!&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.880
SCP-096: The Shy Guy &amp;&nbsp;
SCP-035: The Possessive Mask.&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.760
We begin with the very duo that inspired&nbsp;
this list. As we all know by this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:03.520
SCP-096 is an indestructible, mindless monster&nbsp;
that is extremely distressed by the idea of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.160
somebody seeing its face. So much so that&nbsp;
it’ll activate the creature’s rage state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:14.240
and result in an instant and gruesome death&nbsp;
for everyone involved. And SCP-035 is an evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.320
mind-controlling mask that constantly&nbsp;
secretes a corrosive black liquid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.760
which gradually breaks down the bodies of anyone&nbsp;
wearing it, forcing it to seek out new hosts.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:29.600
If 096 and 035 entered a symbiotic relationship,&nbsp;
it’d be curtains for the rest of us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.600
as they enhance each other’s strengths&nbsp;
and neutralize each other’s weaknesses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.680
096 is unstoppable but mindless, and&nbsp;
035 has a diabolically brilliant mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.400
with no permanent body. Wearing 035, 096 would no&nbsp;
longer need to worry about anyone seeing its face.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.360
The body would also regenerate faster&nbsp;
than 035’s corrosive slime could melt it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.080
resulting in a host that it could presumably&nbsp;
keep forever. With intellect, psychic powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.520
and raw strength and speed, there’d truly&nbsp;
be no stopping this horrible abomination.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.560
SCP-106: The Old Man &amp; SCP-303: The Doorman.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.320
These two are the wingmen from hell, working in&nbsp;
tandem to ensure the ultimate combinations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:18.480
fear, pain, and suffering. 106, the monstrous Old&nbsp;
Man, is a pure sadist that can walk through walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.240
and loves to take his time torturing his hapless&nbsp;
victims with reckless abandon. He’s methodical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.480
but slow, meaning there’s at least a&nbsp;
chance for escape in the short term.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.640
SCP-303, the Doorman, is a&nbsp;
far more mysterious beast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:38.080
He appears behind doors and induces a sense of&nbsp;
paralytic terror within his victims, making them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.440
physically unable to open the door until he&nbsp;
materializes to go mess with somebody else.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.600
Picture this: You’re just chilling in your&nbsp;
bedroom, loving life, when you hear a fizzling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:53.440
sound. You look up to see that it’s SCP-106,&nbsp;
his grinning face melting through the wall.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.240
Immediately, fight or flight kicks in, but you&nbsp;
know you’re not fighting this guy. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.360
running can’t save you this time. You try to make&nbsp;
it to the door, but it’s too late. You’re boxed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.720
in. You can see that freakish, grinning langolier&nbsp;
on the other side, and even with the horror of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.000
Old Man on your tail, you just cannot summon&nbsp;
the will to overcome the fear and leave.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.200
It’s perfect - For them, at least. As the Old&nbsp;
Man gets to really take his time with you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.040
knowing that escape was never really an&nbsp;
option, and we’re sure 303 just likes to watch.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.640
SCP-049: The Plague Doctor&nbsp;
&amp; SCP-1765: The Sisters.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.680
A scientific mind can be a wonderful thing&nbsp;
- When it’s used for good. However, when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.080
apply the cold, scientific methodologies&nbsp;
of a scientist to the pursuit of evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.400
you will often find a far greater depravity&nbsp;
than anything summoned up by a violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.160
barbarian or brute. That’s where this deadly&nbsp;
combo comes into play. The Plague Doctor is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.440
self-proclaimed man of medical science, intent&nbsp;
on curing The Pestilence whenever he sees it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.840
but funnily enough, this seems to mostly involve&nbsp;
killing people and turning them into zombies.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.680
The Sisters, similarly, are a group of spectral&nbsp;
reality warpers with strong beliefs that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.520
twisted games are actually marvelous feats of&nbsp;
science. Like 049, they see themselves as peers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.720
to the SCP Foundation, collecting valuable&nbsp;
data. If ever these so-called scientists got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:22.240
chatting and decided to compare notes, the result&nbsp;
would be not only a truly terrifying brain trust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.280
but some of the most twisted and terrifying&nbsp;
experiments that humankind has ever witnessed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:32.960
And of course, in their own warped minds, it would&nbsp;
all be done in the service of the greater good.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:39.520
SCP-682: The Hard to Destroy Reptile&nbsp;
&amp; SCP-058: The Heart of Darkness.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.400
Sometimes, the best way to make a new friend is&nbsp;
through a common interest. Such as just loving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.840
malicious destruction in its purest forms. The&nbsp;
Hard to Destroy Reptile and the Heart of Darkness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.440
both seem to hate pretty much everything except&nbsp;
causing mass chaos, which they’re both extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.400
good at. But we think that they could be even&nbsp;
better at it if they were working together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:06.240
682 is able to adapt to and reverse any attack&nbsp;
used against it, and tear through Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:12.240
personnel like a tissue in a paper shredder. 058&nbsp;
takes real joy in trampling, whipping things to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.280
death with its spiked tendrils, and firing&nbsp;
flaming acid out of its scorpion stinger.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.400
Couple this with the fact that both&nbsp;
are pretty much indestructible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.920
and you’ve got a duo that could really paint the&nbsp;
town red - with everyone else’s blood. Considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.400
how extremely difficult it is to wrangle even&nbsp;
one of these monsters, the Foundation would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:36.080
need to deploy everything they have to handle a&nbsp;
dual containment breach. And even then, it’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:42.000
real coin toss as to whether any of them would&nbsp;
even be able to stop this duo of evil monsters.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.440
SCP-173: The Sculpture &amp;&nbsp;
SCP-268: The Cap of Neglect.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.600
Let’s leave team-ups behind for a second&nbsp;
and go back to this video’s roots:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:56.000
An iconic anomaly with a piece of headgear&nbsp;
that makes them way more dangerous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:04.560
In this case, it’s SCP-173, the Sculpture, with&nbsp;
SCP-268, the Cap of Neglect. SCP-173 is the OG,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.640
and it’ll treat your neck like a wishbone&nbsp;
if you don’t give it constant attention.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.760
This is where a certain cursed newsboy&nbsp;
cap comes in: 268 is a cap that basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:19.680
makes you impossible to pay attention to, and its&nbsp;
effects only get stronger the longer you wear it.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.440
Eventually, this leads to the&nbsp;
wearer becoming a kind of unperson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.680
simply impossible to interact with,&nbsp;
even when the cap is taken off.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.600
Of course, while this would be a complete&nbsp;
existential nightmare for a human being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:38.800
wearing it, it’d be an absolute dream for SCP-173.&nbsp;
After absorbing the Cap of Neglect’s powers, 173&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:44.000
would become a truly unstoppable killing machine.&nbsp;
Only direct and constant attention would be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:49.680
to keep 173 paralyzed, so when it’s physically&nbsp;
impossible to pay any kind of attention to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.080
it also becomes impossible to stop.&nbsp;
It could snap itself across the globe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.280
and there’s nothing that&nbsp;
any of us could do about it.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.320
SCP-993: Bobble The Clown &amp; SCP-2030: Laugh Is Fun

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:06.480
Who doesn’t love a good crossover, right?&nbsp;
Remember when you watched cartoons as a kid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.200
how exciting it’d be when a&nbsp;
crossover special came on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.840
and you got to see all your favorite characters&nbsp;
from different shows interacting with each other?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:19.760
That’s why we’re proposing the true TV event of&nbsp;
the century: The Bobble the Clown and Laugh Is Fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.960
crossover. This pair of anomalous TV shows are&nbsp;
plenty frightening on their own - Bobble being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:30.400
a clown that makes kids do terrible things, and&nbsp;
Laugh Is Fun being a hidden camera prank show that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:36.320
makes your worst nightmares real - the two of them&nbsp;
together would make you laugh so hard you scream!

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:42.240
We predict that this laugh riot might turn into an&nbsp;
actual riot. Perhaps, with their combined powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.200
they could double their audience, and also&nbsp;
double the sinister effects of their broadcasts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.920
Needless to say, if ever these two did team&nbsp;
up for this incredible piece of television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.680
you’d see a notable uptick in&nbsp;
murders wherever it was broadcast.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:02.800
SCP-4153: It Came from Site-19 &amp;&nbsp;
SCP-701: The Hanged King’s Tragedy

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.280
There’s a well-known phrase in the&nbsp;
performing arts, “The show must go on.”

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:12.400
And this is certainly a very nice sentiment,&nbsp;
unless the players are a selection of living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.720
wax mannequins with a major dramatic&nbsp;
streak, and the play is an eldritch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.920
horror that causes chaos and madness&nbsp;
wherever and whenever it’s performed.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:27.040
That’s right: SCP-4153 is a&nbsp;
selection of living wax thespians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:32.960
modeled after famous universal movie monsters,&nbsp;
and also iconic character actor Vincent Price,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:36.320
and while they typically work on the&nbsp;
haunted house circuit, they’d love to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.280
hit the real stage - Even if the heat of the&nbsp;
footlights makes them go a little droopy.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.200
And what would be a better play for&nbsp;
these dramatic unkillable weirdos than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:51.280
the legendary Carolinian classic, The Hanged&nbsp;
King’s Tragedy? It always brings the house down&nbsp;

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:58.240
into an orgy of terror and bloodshed. Considering&nbsp;
that, unlike most non-anomalous players, SCP-4153&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:03.040
may actually survive their first performance&nbsp;
of the tragedy, they’d be free to perform it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:11.200
again and again and again, racking up more bodies&nbsp;
each time. But like we said, the show must go on…

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:16.800
SCP-3280: After The Storm &amp; SCP-009: Red Ice.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.280
A wise timelord once said, “Water always wins.”&nbsp;
After all, you can’t even really kill water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.720
you can only change its form - And even then,&nbsp;
only temporarily. It’ll always come back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:34.720
It’s in us and all around us. When water goes&nbsp;
rogue, there’s truly no way of fighting back. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:40.320
for that reason that SCP-3280, the nightmarish&nbsp;
living water dubbed After the Storm, is so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:48.480
terrifying. But we know how we could make it even&nbsp;
more dangerous: Mixing it with SCP-009, Red Ice.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.520
This chemically-impossible nightmare converts&nbsp;
into ice crystals as its temperature rises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:59.120
meaning that it getting inside a human body is a&nbsp;
death sentence, as it turns into flesh-rending ice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:04.640
crystals. If you couple the even more deadly&nbsp;
nature of SCP-009 into the frightening speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:10.640
and intelligence of SCP-3280, and they reach&nbsp;
their combined goal of entering the water cycle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.840
then an XK-Class End of the World&nbsp;
Scenario is basically an inevitability.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:23.120
SCP-5049: Demon Dan’s Discount Homonculus&nbsp;
Depot &amp; SCP-1879: Indoor Salesman.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.880
We’d like to start this entry by pouring&nbsp;
one out for the original Demon Dan.&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.920
As fans of our first video on him may recall,&nbsp;
his mysterious demonic superiors blew up his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.080
head after he was captured by the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation to prevent him from giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:41.040
up sensitive information. We imagine this kind&nbsp;
of thing happens a lot, and it results in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.480
Discount Homonculus Depot needing new, go-getting&nbsp;
salesmen to move products and meet quotas.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:54.560
Enter SCP-1879, the Indoor Salesman, and ultimate&nbsp;
hard bargain driver. He’s underappreciated at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:59.840
his old job and looking for work. That might&nbsp;
lead to him getting headhunted by SCP-5049,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.800
and with the increased power given to him&nbsp;
by the Demon Lords, his operation will move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.320
from just covering Washington to popping up&nbsp;
anywhere and everywhere - And what’s more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:15.120
he might now have a whole new gaggle of&nbsp;
Impish assistants. With that kind of setup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:24.160
we can only imagine he’d be a Helluva Boss.
SCP-4666: The Yule Man &amp; SCP-784: Christmas Cheer.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:29.360
Are you longing for the holidays? Do you wish it&nbsp;
could be Christmas every day? Trust us, you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.880
not the only one. Our good friend, the terrifying,&nbsp;
sadistic Yule Man, also wishes for a little more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:39.440
Christmas - Considering he can only actually&nbsp;
operate during twelve days out of the year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:44.960
However, this wouldn’t be the case if he made&nbsp;
himself a new home just outside of SCP-784:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.560
The neighborhood where it really&nbsp;
is Christmas every single day!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:52.320
Here, it presumably stands to reason&nbsp;
that these two anomalies could form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:57.680
a terrifying symbiotic relationship, where the&nbsp;
Yule Man could operate on any day of the year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:03.440
becoming significantly more dangerous and&nbsp;
taking lives - or worse - whenever he feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:08.880
like it. It’s safe to say, if the Yule Man&nbsp;
decided to set up a new grotto in SCP-784,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.640
he’d be the only one experiencing&nbsp;
some Christmas cheer around here…

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:18.480
SCP-076-2: Able &amp; SCP-4955: Knife.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.800
If there are three things that you know about&nbsp;
Able, it’s probably these three things: He’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.840
got a potentially biblical backstory, he comes&nbsp;
out of a giant stone coffin, and he’s really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:32.720
really good with edged weaponry. Able can&nbsp;
actually produce his own blades from thin air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:36.880
yanking them out of pocket dimensions&nbsp;
whenever he needs them. But personally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:43.920
we think he’d be even more dangerous if he got&nbsp;
his hands on SCP-4955, also known simply as KNIFE.

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:50.240
KNIFE is an interesting anomaly. Initially thought&nbsp;
to have antimemetic properties - Seeing as nobody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.800
except the user is able to acknowledge it, or&nbsp;
anything it does - but the reality is that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.800 --> 00:13:00.720
has even more bizarre memetic properties. The&nbsp;
KNIFE forces everyone except the user to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.840
their part in a huge practical joke where&nbsp;
everybody pretends to not notice the knife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:11.840
or its actions in order to gaslight the user.&nbsp;
However, if the KNIFE was in Able’s hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:15.920
the joke would definitely be on&nbsp;
them. He’d be the perfect assassin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:21.040
cutting down scores of victims while nobody could&nbsp;
even acknowledge that he was the perpetrator.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:27.360
SCP-001: The Gate Guardian &amp;&nbsp;
SCP-1179: The Centralian Fire Demon.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.880
Friends need to have things in&nbsp;
common to make a friendship work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:35.600
After all, common interests are often&nbsp;
the basis for all engaging conversations.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:41.280
That’s why it stands to reason that the giant,&nbsp;
flaming warrior known as SCP-001 The Gate Guardian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:47.680
would probably get along famously with the giant,&nbsp;
flaming warrior known as SCP-1179 The Centralian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:53.760
Fire Demon. This devoted soldier of angelic light&nbsp;
and his new cantankerous balrog buddy would likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:58.880
have a lot to say to each other, and become&nbsp;
an almost unstoppable fighting duo together.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:03.840
They’re both ancient, impossibly large,&nbsp;
with immensely powerful flame-based weaponry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:09.760
and presumably a fair bit of battle knowledge. It&nbsp;
would take a truly special enemy to take on these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:15.200
two together and even survive, let alone win!&nbsp;
Between them, they might even stand a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:20.560
against other impossibly large enemies like&nbsp;
The Devourer of Worlds. And, if nothing else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:26.320
it would likely be an incredible fight to witness&nbsp;
unfold - Even if you died immediately after.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:31.600
SCP-2094: Motormouth &amp; SCP-323: Wendigo Skull.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.040
And so we once again return&nbsp;
to this video’s mainstay:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:40.560
An already powerful anomaly being made far more&nbsp;
dangerous by a piece of anomalous headwear. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:47.040
are nothing if not consistent, folks. Admittedly,&nbsp;
SCP-2094, also known by his circus stage name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.600
Motormouth, isn’t exactly an aggressive&nbsp;
anomaly. He’s a reasonable, chatty guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:56.720
who just happens to have an impossibly stretchy&nbsp;
jaw and a seemingly limitless pocket dimension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:01.200
in his stomach. All good stuff if you’re&nbsp;
in the mood for some bizarre party tricks.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:05.840
However, this becomes a lot more&nbsp;
sinister if he’s made to wear SCP-323,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:11.120
also known as the Wendigo Skull. This cursed&nbsp;
skull is imbued with the spirit of the legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:17.440
Algonquin monster known as the Wendigo, a beast so&nbsp;
dangerous that even saying its name can be risky.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:22.800
In putting on the skull, the wearer is possessed&nbsp;
and descends into a state of violent cannibalism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:26.480
Of course, this is bad enough on its&nbsp;
own, but on someone like Motormouth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.200
where there’s no real ceiling&nbsp;
on what he’s capable of eating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:34.320
the skull could force him to devour thousands&nbsp;
of people. He’d go from a charming circus act&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:41.440
to a hungry weapon of mass destruction in no&nbsp;
time, making these two a deadly SCP combination.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.960
SCP-4973: Dead Men &amp; SCP-2419: The Laughing Men.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:51.760
“Well, well, well, if it isn’t the&nbsp;
consequences of my own actions,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.520
is probably what the Foundation thought when&nbsp;
first discovering both SCP-4973, the Dead Men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:03.920
and SCP-2419, the Laughing Men. That’s because&nbsp;
these two groups have something in common:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:08.560
They’re the ghoulish remnants of D-Classes&nbsp;
killed under Foundation watch, and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:14.240
in their horrible post-death states, they’ve got&nbsp;
a real ax to grind with their former tormentors.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:20.080
SCP-4973 are frightening ghosts that get revenge&nbsp;
on the researchers who experimented on them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:24.560
and 2419 are a set of laughing physical&nbsp;
abominations that resulted from all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:29.200
happy memories being extracted from&nbsp;
D-Class corpses for use in amnestic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:34.080
production. If these two teamed up, they’d&nbsp;
be a deadly and terrifying anti-Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:39.600
force that would likely leave mountains of&nbsp;
SCP Foundation corpses lying in their wake.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:45.840
SCP-507: The Reluctant Dimension&nbsp;
Hopper &amp; SCP-2935: O, Death.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:50.080
Here’s a not-so-fun fact we’ve all learned in&nbsp;
the past few years: When somebody goes somewhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:54.320
they shouldn’t, then brings something&nbsp;
infectious back, it’s bad for everyone.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:58.800
And nobody goes to more places&nbsp;
he shouldn’t than SCP-507,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:03.040
also known as the Reluctant Dimension&nbsp;
Hopper. Though in the poor guy’s defense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.680
he really doesn’t choose where to go, thanks&nbsp;
to his random teleportation ability. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:13.840
if this resulted in a sudden trip to SCP-2935,&nbsp;
an alternate dimension nicknamed O, Death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:18.000
it would in turn result in the deadliest&nbsp;
anomalous combination of all time.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.080
You see, 2935 is infected with&nbsp;
the spirit of death itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.520
wiping out all life on every&nbsp;
level - Even being the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:31.840
being in all recorded realities capable of&nbsp;
instantly and permanently killing SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.040
And this spirit of death takes emissaries to&nbsp;
spread it across dimensions, wiping out everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:42.960
as it goes and using Foundation distress signals&nbsp;
to lure in its next unwitting harbinger of death.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:47.120
The Foundation has blocked off the one physical&nbsp;
entrance to this dimension in our world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:51.440
but nothing is stopping 507 from&nbsp;
being reluctantly teleported there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:57.200
And when he gets back, believe us, he’ll be&nbsp;
bringing an interesting new friend with him…

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:01.680
And there you have it, folks, the combos&nbsp;
that’ll break you. What was your favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:06.240
deadly combination of SCPs we covered today?&nbsp;
And do you have any ideas for killer combos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:11.200
that we didn’t cover in this video? Let us&nbsp;
know down in the comments. And remember, kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.840
when it comes to dangerous anomalies,&nbsp;
teamwork makes the nightmare work.

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:21.760
Now go check out “Worst Ways to Die - SCP&nbsp;
Edition” and “SCP-999 Tickle Monster VS. the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:27.840
Most Evil SCPs” for more truly superlative&nbsp;
anomalous experiences from SCP Explained!

